Slippi's HTTP services in the engine's netplay object (mu-engine/patches/net-0004; Melee-NX-NetPlay's patches/net-0008, as
Slippi Dolphin 3.7.0 and melee-unlocked use them):
- Display name refresh: after sign-in the netplay object asks Slippi's user service for the account's display name, connect
  code, latest version and chat messages (Slippi Dolphin's overwriteFromServer, melee-unlocked's User::RefreshFromServer), on a
  thread of its own; user.json is never written, and a failed request keeps what user.json says. Never with a local peer.
- Replay upload: when the game report's reply carries uploadUrl, the replay is asked for on the reporter's thread then
  (slippi::last_replay_path, the engine's replay writer), not on the game thread when the game reports.
- Tests only: MELEE_SERVICES_LOOPBACK_PORT points these requests at the loopback stand-in (tools/mac/mock_slippi_http.py);
  only http://127.0.0.1:<port> can be chosen that way.
The report's disc MD5 (isoHash, cached in iso_md5_cache.txt) is this repository's reporter as before. Applied by ../net_sources.sh.

